<article class="env-definition" id="00Z4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00Z4">Definition <span data-tag="00Z4">7.47.6</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category. A <em>topology on $\mathcal{C}$</em> is given by a rule which assigns to every $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ a subset $J(U)$ of the set of all sieves on $U$ satisfying the following conditions </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
For every morphism $f : V \to U$ in $\mathcal{C}$, and every element $S \in J(U)$ the pullback $S \times _ U V$ is an element of $J(V)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $S$ and $S'$ are sieves on $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$, if $S \in J(U)$, and if for all $f \in S(V)$ the pullback $S' \times _ U V$ belongs to $J(V)$, then $S'$ belongs to $J(U)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
For every $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ the maximal sieve $S = h_ U$ belongs to $J(U)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
